Asparagus Amandine
Serves: 5
Prep: 10 min
Cook: 15 min
Total: 25 min
Source: Adapted from Serious Eats' haricots verts amandine
Equipment: Large pot or deep frying pan, Bowl of iced water, Tongs, Medium skillet, Kitchen towels

Toss (heat): Add the asparagus and toss until **hot and glossy**. Season.
  Emulsify (heat, 30 s): Add the lemon juice and **{1–2 Tbsp} water**. High heat; shake the pan hard until the sauce is **glossy**.
    Toast (heat, ~7 min): Butter and almonds over **medium-low**, stirring, until **deeply browned**, ~5 min. Add garlic and shallot; **2 min** more.
      - 35 g = 3 Tbsp | Unsalted butter
      - 85 g = 3 oz | Slivered almonds
      Slice: Peel and thinly slice.
        - 2 cloves | Garlic
        - 1 | Shallots
    Squeeze: Juice the lemon.
      - 1 | Lemon | for 1½ Tbsp juice
  Blanch (heat, 2–4 min, then set aside): Snap off the woody ends. Into well-salted boiling water until **just tender**, **2 min** thin, **3–4 min** thick, then straight into iced water. Drain and dry well.
    - 650 g = 1½ lb | Green asparagus | medium spears
    - for the water | Kosher salt
    - plenty | Ice
